  "id": "COMPOUND:4783 - PROTEIN:3049",
  "verbalization": "Pleconaril appears to interact with Cytochrome c4 through a series of target relationships, with G1/S-specific cyclin-D1 acting as a common intermediary. This cyclin-D1 is targeted by two distinct compounds: 6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin and 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin, both of which have their own specific targets, including Cytochrome c4. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Cytochrome c4 suggests a potential role in the cellular response to these compounds. The integration of these pathways implies that Pleconaril may influence cellular processes through the activation of cyclin-D1, which in turn modulates the activity of Cytochrome c4. The evidence supports a mechanism where Pleconaril could indirectly affect Cytochrome c4 by targeting cyclin-D1, highlighting a possible regulatory role in cellular signaling pathways.",
